/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/8/code.py:22:#     ORANGE(7): already-spent charge
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/8/code.py:23:#     GREY(5): 1-step charge, turns into ORANGE when consumed
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/8/code.py:24:#     BLUE(1): 2-step weighted obstacle, never changes color
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/8/code.py:26:#   some head-side bands are ORANGE, and the remaining bands are a BLUE/GREY mix with at least one
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/8/code.py:27:#   BLUE band before a later GREY band. This keeps the scene tidy while making "skip blue, fill grey"
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/8/code.py:32:# - A 1x4 interior `[ORANGE, BLUE, GREY, BLUE]` has:
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/8/code.py:37:#     original task: steps = min(4, 1) = 1, so the container would move 1 and the GREY would turn ORANGE
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/8/code.py:40:#     only the GREY cell is consumable, so it becomes ORANGE
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/8/code.py:41:#     both BLUE cells stay BLUE even though they contributed 4 weighted steps together
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/8/code.py:44:#     BLUE affects distance computation but not recoloring
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/8/code.py:47:# - The extra role is fixed to BLUE rather than per-object color remapping, so examples stay readable.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/8/code.py:50:# - It also forces at least one mover with BLUE before a later GREY band, so solvers must infer that
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/8/code.py:51:#   BLUE is not just decoration and that GREY filling skips over BLUE obstacles.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/8/code.py:57:# - Original container detection started from connected `(GREY | ORANGE)` regions. That breaks here
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/8/code.py:58:#   because BLUE can separate those regions. The fused solver therefore detects black rectangular
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/8/code.py:60:# - Original head detection excluded only background / border / grey / orange. With BLUE inside the
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/8/code.py:61:#   frame, border-adjacent BLUE would be mistaken for a head seed unless BLUE is excluded too.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/8/code.py:64:# - D10/2's single-variant logic would additionally recolor BLUE through BLUE->GREY->ORANGE. That is
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/8/code.py:65:#   explicitly wrong for this combo: BLUE contributes weight but stays BLUE.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/8/code.py:78:# - Because some BLUE stripes sit before later GREY stripes, outputs visibly show GREY farther inward
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/8/code.py:79:#   turning ORANGE while closer BLUE remains BLUE.
